# Languages the editor ships

The editor carries a grammar for each language on this card, so every body
here is coloured in a window with no other extension. Each language appears
as a plain fence and as a cell.

## Python

```python
from dataclasses import dataclass

@dataclass
class Language:
    name: str
    year: int

def age(language: Language, in_year: int = 2026) -> int:
    """The age of a language in a given year."""
    return in_year - language.year
```

```python#eval id=ages
ages = {l.name: age(l) for l in [Language("Python", 1991), Language("Rust", 2015)]}
print(f"{len(ages)} languages, oldest {max(ages.values())} years")
```

## TypeScript

```ts
interface Language { name: string; year: number }

export const age = (l: Language, inYear = 2026): number => inYear - l.year;
```

```typescript#eval hidden
const oldest = [{ name: "Python", year: 1991 }].map((l) => age(l)).sort()[0];
```

## Rust

```rust
#[derive(Debug)]
struct Language<'a> { name: &'a str, year: u16 }

impl Language<'_> {
    fn age(&self, in_year: u16) -> u16 { in_year - self.year }
}
```

```rs#check id=borrow
let python = Language { name: "Python", year: 1991 };
println!("{python:?} is {} years old", python.age(2026));
```

## Go

```go#eval
package main

import "fmt"

func main() { fmt.Printf("%d years\n", 2026-1991) }
```

## C and C++

```c#eval
#include <stdio.h>
int main(void) { printf("%d years\n", 2026 - 1991); return 0; }
```

```c++#eval
#include <iostream>
template <typename T> T age(T year) { return 2026 - year; }
int main() { std::cout << age(1991) << " years\n"; }
```

## C#

`c#` with nothing after it is the language C#. `c#eval` is a cell in C.

```c#
record Language(string Name, int Year) { public int Age => 2026 - Year; }
```

## Java

```java#eval
record Language(String name, int year) { int age() { return 2026 - year; } }
```

## Shell

```bash#eval id=count
for f in catalog/*.hmd; do echo "${f%.hmd}"; done | wc -l
```

```sh
grep -l "grammar: install" catalog/*.hmd
```

## SQL

```sql#eval
SELECT name, 2026 - year AS age FROM languages WHERE typing = 'static' ORDER BY age DESC;
```

## Data

```json#eval
{ "name": "HQL", "year": 2026, "typed": true, "aliases": ["hql"], "note": null }
```

```yaml#eval id=header
title: HQL
metadata: { year: 2026, typing: static }
tags: [language, typed]
```

```xml
<language name="HQL" year="2026"><alias>hql</alias></language>
```

## The web

```html#eval
<table class="catalog"><tr><th>Language</th><td data-year="2026">HQL</td></tr></table>
```

```css
.catalog td[data-year="2026"] { color: #0a7; font-weight: 600; }
```

```javascript#eval
document.querySelectorAll(".catalog td").forEach((td) => console.log(td.dataset.year));
```

## Other built-in grammars

```diff
-  "meta.embedded.block.yaml": "yaml"
+  "meta.embedded.block.hql": "hql",
```

```dockerfile
FROM rust:1.83 AS build
RUN cargo install hql --locked
```

```makefile
grammar: syntaxes/fences.mjs
	node syntaxes/fences.mjs
```

```lua#eval
local year = 1993; print(2026 - year)
```

```ruby#eval
puts %w[python rust].map(&:capitalize).join(", ")
```

```php
<?php echo 2026 - 1995, " years\n";
```

```swift
struct Language { let name: String; let year: Int }
```

```powershell
Get-ChildItem catalog -Filter *.hmd | Measure-Object
```

```ini
[discovery]
autodiscovery = true
```
